<title>UK: Emerald to start Colombian drilling.</title>
<headline>Emerald to start Colombian drilling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emerald Energy Plc, the UK independent energy explorer, said on Friday it expects to start its first well in its Colombian drilling programme on March 10.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it has contracted a rig, which will drill the Chawina 2 well, on the Apulo Block, 60 kilometres west of Bogata.</p>
<p>The well has an estimated target depth of 8,500 feet and will take around 35 days to complete.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
